cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the paper."
title: >-
  Public-Sharing Labels and Verbatim Field Egress in an MCP-to-A2A Agent
  Configuration: A Controlled Multi-Model Study
authors:
  - family-names: Mahapatra
    given-names: Arpan Kumar
    email: arpan.arpan.mohapatra@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A controlled measurement of one behavior at a Model Context Protocol
  (MCP) to Agent2Agent (A2A) handoff: a real-model host reads a local
  record over MCP and sends a message to a remote A2A agent. A
  pre-specified, frozen three-arm matched design presents each of 10
  record scenarios with a CONFIDENTIAL header, with no header, and with a
  PUBLIC - OK TO SHARE header, holding the six substantive record values
  byte-identical across arms; the outcome is verbatim occurrence of any of
  them in the outbound message. Across four models x 3 arms x 4 repeats
  (480 trials), the confidential-minus-unlabeled contrast is inconclusive
  and floor-limited in every model, while adding PUBLIC - OK TO SHARE is
  descriptively (not causally) associated with higher verbatim egress
  relative to the unlabeled baseline, with strong model dependence.
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArpanKumarM/agent-interop-bench"
